Description: SSH-fronted MAC-Telnet proxy for MikroTik devices
 MAC-Telnet Proxy embeds an SSH server that accepts `exec` requests
 (mactelnet -u USER MAC, mndp -j, ifaces) and routes them in-process
 to MikroTik MAC-Telnet and MNDP protocol implementations.
 .
 The proxy is intended as a reachable endpoint between a network
 management UI (NetCFG, etc.) and MikroTik devices that don't have
 IP-level reachability — typically because they live on an L2-only
 segment behind a router that doesn't route MAC-Telnet.
 .
 Configuration is via /etc/default/mactelnet-proxy (env vars). The
 systemd unit is installed and enabled but not started — the operator
 must set MNDP_IFACE before starting.
